WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:04.920
What's up everybody! This is Zacky from
Geek Culture and today we will be

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:10.680
unboxing the Star Wars - The Vintage
Collection: The Mandalorian AT-ST Raider toy vehicle.

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:15.440
This AT-ST Raider toy is
inspired by the vehicles in The Mandalorian.

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:19.540
The upcoming series premiering on Disney+ on November 12 this year.

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:23.550
Not much is known about the
series so far. Though we know it will

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:27.689
take place five years after the events
of Return of the Jedi and follows the

00:00:27.689 --> 00:00:30.680
journey of a Mandalorian bounty hunter.

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:34.300
First and foremost is the
vintage-inspired packaging itself.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:37.060
It features the original Kenner toys branding

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:40.739
Which has produced several highly recognizable
toys and merchandise

00:00:40.739 --> 00:00:44.460
some of you may remember the action
figures from the original series of Star Wars and

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:46.700
and Jurassic Park.

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:53.220
Out of the box we
get a disassembled AT-ST and a Klatooinian AT-ST pilot.

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:56.760
Now not much is known
about how Klatooine and The Mandalorian fits

00:00:56.760 --> 00:01:02.000
into the story but what we can say is that
this variant of the All-Terrain Scout Transport Vehicle

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:07.760
is used by a Klatooinian Raider
after the fall of the Galactic Empire.

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:12.040
The Klatooinian AT-ST Raider
features an opening cockpit,

00:01:12.049 --> 00:01:17.880
articulated legs, adjustable laser cannons,

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:26.080
side-mounted weapon pods and moveable
command viewpoint blast shield.

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:31.100
This AT-ST also sports a new paint job that we
will probably see in the show.

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:37.100
Customized with Klatooinian decals and paintwork
fabric material and a net.

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:39.800
It just goes to show how
much detail it went to make this figure

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:42.040
and leaves us speculating for what is to come.

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:46.780
And it's also compatible
with 3.75-inch scale Star Wars action figures.

00:01:46.799 --> 00:01:51.030
and what a better way than to
show it off with the figurines from the

00:01:51.030 --> 00:01:57.509
Commemorative Edition Skywalker Saga.
These are the first wave of 3.75-inch gold

00:01:57.509 --> 00:02:00.420
figure 2 packs in this new series.

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:03.200
Right out of the bat, there's a metallic foil

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:07.619
packaging on the print if you flip to
the back each of these boxes have their

00:02:07.619 --> 00:02:13.170
respective prints from the prequel
trilogy; Episode 1: The Phantom Menace in 1999

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:18.390
which features Darth Maul and Yoda.
Episode 2: Attack of the clones in 2002,

00:02:18.390 --> 00:02:24.900
with Mace Windu and Jango Fett, and Episode 3 Revenge of the Sith in 2005 with

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:27.940
Obi-Wan and Anakin Skywalker.

00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:32.140
With that we hope you enjoyed this unboxing of the Klatoonian AT-ST Raider toy

00:02:32.140 --> 00:02:34.980
and the figures for the Skywalker saga.

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:38.400
If you would like to know more about these goodies
be sure to check out the link in the

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:42.329
description below don't forget to slam
that subscribe button and tell us about

00:02:42.329 --> 00:02:44.620
what you would like us to unbox next.

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:46.440
See you on the next one!

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:48.440
Until then, stay geeky!

